--- body ---
Categorized findings from full read of all 26 production files and 7 test
files. go vet clean, 177 tests pass. Findings grouped by category.

## Dead code (low)
1. HasMagic field on Erg — set by parser, never read in production; only
   consumed by test assertions.
2. type Line = string — type alias (not definition), zero compile-time
   safety; semantic noise.

## Duplication (medium)
3. ownerRE and repoRE in ergspecv1.go are byte-identical regexps.
4. validTagValues (ergspecv1.go) and skipReadyTags (ready.go) are
   independently defined maps with the same keys.
5. Three ID-from-filename extractors: parseIDFromFilename (int),
   FilenameID (string), globLocalIDs (inline split).

## Consistency (low–medium)
6. filepath.Walk (deprecated) in migrate.go and check.go vs
   filepath.WalkDir (modern) in nextid.go and ready.go.
7. TestClosedWhitespaceDivergence documents parseHeaderLine vs
   isClosedHeaderLine whitespace inconsistency — pins divergence
   instead of fixing it.

## Efficiency (medium)
8. removeBlockedByRef in close.go loads entire corpus via loadErgs to
   find files referencing a given ID, then re-reads each matching file
   line-by-line to edit it. Single pass possible.

## Test gaps (high–medium)
9. migrate.go (~344 lines) — complex multi-pass rewrite logic with zero
   unit tests. migrateFile is pure (bytes in -> bytes out), table-drivable.
10. No unit tests for cmdLog, cmdArchive, cmdReady, cmdCheck, cmdVersion,
    cmdUpdate, cmdInit. Priority: cmdReady and cmdCheck (most logic).
11. globLocalIDs (validate.go) has no direct test.

## Design / fragility (medium–low)
12. Positional struct literal at ready.go:272 (readyEntry{...}).
13. bootstrap_assets.go uses hand-rolled base64 instead of //go:embed.

## File organization (medium)
14. erg.go mixes type declarations (Line, Erg, Ref-adjacent helpers) with
    parser logic and spec constants (v1HeaderKeys, v1SingletonKeys, inline
    separator literals). ergspecv1.go already holds spec constants but the
    split is incomplete — types and remaining constants should consolidate
    into ergspecv1.go, leaving erg.go as pure parser/method code.

## Actions (quick-fix PR scope)

In-scope findings: #1, #2, #3, #6, #12, #13, #14. Commit order follows
dependency (types first, then callers).

### A1. Remove HasMagic from Erg struct (#1)

Verified: HasMagic is set in parseErgBytes (erg.go:440) and in the struct
literal (erg.go:23). Production code never reads it. 8 test assertions in
erg_test.go read it as a proxy for "parser detected magic line."

Actions:
- Delete `HasMagic bool` from the Erg struct (erg.go:23).
- Delete `HasMagic: hasMagic,` from the struct literal (erg.go:440).
  The local `hasMagic` variable stays — it drives rule 1 error emission.
- Rewrite 8 test assertions in erg_test.go: replace `erg.HasMagic`
  checks with assertions on `parseErrs` content — presence/absence of
  the string `"missing magic first line"`. This is the observable
  behavior, not an internal field.

### A2. Remove type Line = string alias (#2)

Verified: `type Line = string` at erg.go:13 is a type alias (=), not a
type definition. The compiler treats Line and string identically — no
type safety. Used only in the Erg struct fields and local variables in
parseErgBytes.

Actions:
- Delete the `type Line = string` declaration and its comment (erg.go:11-13).
- Replace all `Line` with `string` in the Erg struct fields (erg.go:22-33)
  and in `var title, created, author, closed Line` (erg.go:183)
  and `var tags []Line` (erg.go:185).

### A3. Merge ownerRE and repoRE into identRE (#3)

Verified: ownerRE (ergspecv1.go:68) and repoRE (ergspecv1.go:75) compile
identical patterns: `^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$`. Single call site: ref.go:76
(`ownerRE.MatchString(owner) && repoRE.MatchString(repo)`).

Actions:
- Replace both declarations with a single `identRE` in ergspecv1.go.
  Comment references the ABNF productions for both owner and repo.
- Update ref.go:76 to `identRE.MatchString(owner) && identRE.MatchString(repo)`.
- Existing tests in ref_test.go cover this end-to-end (no new tests needed).

### A4. Replace filepath.Walk with filepath.WalkDir (#6)

Verified: filepath.Walk call sites are:
- erg.go:485 (loadErgs) — uses `os.FileInfo`
- migrate.go:68 (cmdMigrate walk) — uses `os.FileInfo`
- migrate.go:321 (hasStatusHeader) — uses `os.FileInfo`

These pass `os.FileInfo` in their walk function signature. filepath.WalkDir
uses `fs.DirEntry` instead, which avoids a stat syscall per entry.

Correction to original finding: check.go does NOT call filepath.Walk
directly — it uses loadErgs (erg.go). The three actual call sites are
all in erg.go and migrate.go.

Actions per call site:
- Change `filepath.Walk` to `filepath.WalkDir` and update the callback
  signature from `func(path string, info os.FileInfo, err error)` to
  `func(path string, d fs.DirEntry, err error)`.
- Replace `info.IsDir()` with `d.IsDir()` and `info.Name()` with
  `d.Name()` (same API on DirEntry).
- Add `"io/fs"` import to erg.go and migrate.go (remove `"os"` if it
  becomes unused — but both files still use os.ReadFile/os.WriteFile).

### A5. Switch positional struct literal to named fields (#12)

Verified: ready.go:272 constructs readyEntry positionally:
  `entry := readyEntry{tid, t.Title, t.Filename(), tags, !blocked, claimed, blockedBy}`

The readyEntry struct (ready.go:18-24) has 7 fields. Any reordering
or insertion breaks this silently.

Action:
- Rewrite to named fields:
  `entry := readyEntry{id: tid, title: t.Title, file: t.Filename(), tags: tags, ready: !blocked, claimed: claimed, blockedBy: blockedBy}`

### A6. Replace hand-rolled base64 with //go:embed (#13)

Verified: bootstrap_assets.go holds 3 assets as base64 strings in a
hand-maintained map. No Makefile target generates it. go.mod requires
Go 1.21, which supports //go:embed. The asset files referenced are:
- tickets/AGENTS.md
- tickets/spec-erg-v1.md
- tickets/integration.md

These paths are relative to the project root, not to src/go/. For
//go:embed, files must be in or below the package directory.

Actions:
- Create directory src/go/assets/ and place the 3 decoded .md files
  there (AGENTS.md, spec-erg-v1.md, integration.md).
- Rewrite bootstrap_assets.go: declare `//go:embed assets/AGENTS.md`,
  etc. using `embed.FS` or individual `string` vars.
- Update bootstrapAsset() to read from the embedded FS.
- Update initAssetPaths in init.go (the lookup keys change from
  `tickets/AGENTS.md` to `assets/AGENTS.md` internally, but the write
  targets stay as `tickets/AGENTS.md`).
- Shell test tests/test_init.sh covers end-to-end asset unpacking.

### A7. Consolidate types and spec constants into ergspecv1.go (#14)

Verified: erg.go currently holds declarations that belong with the spec:
- `type Line = string` (removed by A2, irrelevant here)
- `Erg` struct definition (lines 15-35)
- `v1HeaderKeys` map (lines 141-144)
- `v1SingletonKeys` map (lines 148-150)
- Separator literals `"--- log ---"` and `"--- body ---"` are inlined
  at 9 code sites across 4 files (erg.go, migrate.go, close.go, new.go)

ergspecv1.go already holds: magicLine, validTagValues, isoDateRE,
filenameRE, logLineRE, hostRE, ownerRE/repoRE.

Actions (three sub-steps):

A7a. Move `Erg` struct definition from erg.go to ergspecv1.go.
  Methods (IsClosed, Filename, FilenameID) stay in erg.go — Go allows
  methods in any file of the same package.

A7b. Move `v1HeaderKeys` and `v1SingletonKeys` from erg.go to
  ergspecv1.go.

A7c. Define `logSeparator` and `bodySeparator` constants in
  ergspecv1.go and replace all inline literals. Code sites to update:
  - erg.go:219   `trimmed == "--- log ---"`
  - erg.go:226   `trimmed == "--- body ---"`
  - migrate.go:234  `strings.TrimSpace(line) == "--- log ---"`
  - migrate.go:271  `strings.TrimSpace(line) == "--- log ---"`
  - migrate.go:333  `strings.TrimSpace(line) == "--- log ---"`
  - close.go:176  `strings.TrimSpace(line) == "--- log ---"`
  - close.go:204  `strings.Index(content, "\n--- body ---")`
  - log.go:77     `strings.Contains(string(data), "\n--- body ---")`
  - new.go:88     inline in template string (use constant concat)
  Test assertions and doc comments that mention the literals stay as-is.

Scope deferral: Ref and RefKind already live in ref.go alongside their
parser (parseRef). Moving them to ergspecv1.go would gut ref.go into a
parser-only file with no type context. Deferred — ref.go is already a
coherent unit.

### Commit order

1. A2 (remove Line alias) — no dependencies, simplest change.
2. A1 (remove HasMagic) — includes test rewrites.
3. A3 (merge ownerRE/repoRE) — standalone.
4. A7 (move Erg struct, v1HeaderKeys, v1SingletonKeys, separator
   constants to ergspecv1.go) — may split into sub-commits if diff
   is large.
5. A4 (filepath.Walk→WalkDir) — standalone.
6. A5 (named struct fields) — standalone.
7. A6 (embed) — last because it creates new files and touches init.go.

### First test to write

After A6, add TestBootstrapAssetContent in erg_test.go (or a new
bootstrap_assets_test.go): for each of the 3 asset paths, call
bootstrapAsset() and assert the returned string starts with the expected
first line (e.g., `# tickets/` for AGENTS.md, `# Ticket format spec` for
spec-erg-v1.md). This catches encoding drift from the embed switch
without being tautological.

Antipattern check — tests to avoid:
- Asserting `identRE.String() == "^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$"` — recompiles
  the regex pattern; catches only a different implementation, not a
  wrong one.
- Asserting "HasMagic field does not exist" — tests the implementation
  shape, not behavior.
- Asserting Erg struct fields list — recompiles the type.

### Out of scope (deferred findings)

- #4 (tag map duplication): absorbed by ticket 0126.
- #5 (3 ID extractors): needs design thought about which to keep.
- #7 (whitespace divergence): needs design decision (align which way).
- #8 (removeBlockedByRef double-parse): medium complexity refactor.
- #9 (migrate.go tests): large scope, separate ticket.
- #10 (command tests): large scope, separate ticket.
- #11 (globLocalIDs test): low priority.
- #14 partial (Ref/RefKind move): ref.go is a coherent unit — type and
  parser together. Moving Ref/RefKind to ergspecv1.go would gut it.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `cd src/go && go vet ./...` clean
- [ ] `cd src/go && go test ./...` passes (177+ tests)
- [ ] `make test` passes (unit + shell integration)
- [ ] No `HasMagic` references outside comments
- [ ] No `type Line =` declaration
- [ ] `ownerRE` and `repoRE` replaced by single `identRE`
- [ ] Zero `filepath.Walk` calls (all replaced by WalkDir)
- [ ] readyEntry literal uses named fields
- [ ] bootstrap_assets.go uses //go:embed, no base64 encoding
- [ ] v1HeaderKeys, v1SingletonKeys live in ergspecv1.go
- [ ] Erg struct definition lives in ergspecv1.go
- [ ] logSeparator, bodySeparator constants in ergspecv1.go; no inline literals
